cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "News Timing Cannot Explain It: replication package"
version: 1.0.0
license: "MIT"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/coderback/zhang2025-replication"
abstract: >-
  Code, pre-registration, FinBERT scores and results for a pre-registered replication of Zhang (2025),
  "Interpretable Machine Learning for Macro Alpha: A News Sentiment Case Study" (arXiv:2505.16136), which
  reports cost-adjusted Sharpe ratios of 4.6 to 5.9 from FinBERT sentiment of GDELT headlines. The
  replication finds Sharpe ratios near zero or negative on every asset, timing and model. Nothing here is
  investment advice.
message: "If you use this package, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - given-names: Timothy Oluwatobi
    family-names: Ojebiyi
    affiliation: Independent researcher
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-7786-8549"
keywords:
  - replication
  - pre-registration
  - news sentiment
  - FinBERT
  - GDELT
  - foreign exchange
  - reproducibility
